// Regression for the stage-2 self-compile OOM: `HashMap.set` on an EXISTING
// key must free the replaced value. The self-hosted codegen leaked it because
// `_find_bucket`'s `bucket := (data_ptr &+ i).*` (a value-struct copy holding
// an RC field) was neither dup'd at the copy site nor dropped on its early
// `return .Some(idx)` path — so every probe hit stole/leaked the map's own
// reference. Since the compiler's `expr_info_table_set` overwrites the same
// expr-ids millions of times during def-time re-eval, that per-overwrite leak
// is what ballooned `s2 compile yo-self/main.yo` until it OOM-killed.
//
// Fix (codegen/exprs/init_assignment.yo): register the scalar `:=` local's C
// name via `get_variable_type_string` (so its scope/early-return drop is not
// skipped) AND dup the raw-deref struct copy at the copy site
// (`generate_dup_code_for_value`), matching TS.
//
// Observable: `Gc.tracked_count()`. `Node` is self-referential (cyclable) so
// each live instance is tracked; the count is kept below the GC's auto-collect
// threshold so the collector cannot mask a missing drop. With the fix the live
// count stays tiny after the overwrite loop (the map holds ONE value); the
// pre-fix leak left ~one live Node per overwrite. The bounded assert PASSES
// identically under the TS reference compiler and the fixed self-hosted binary
// (both print "hashmap-overwrite ok"); a regression re-introducing the leak
// trips the assert (non-zero exit / DIFF in the differential harness).
{ assert } :: import("std/assert");
{ println } :: import("std/fmt");
Gc :: import("std/gc");
{ HashMap } :: import("std/collections/hash_map");

Node :: ref(struct(x : i32, next : Option(Self)));

main :: (fn() -> unit)({
  m := HashMap(i32, Node).new();
  (j : i32) = i32(0);
  while(j < i32(64), {
    m.set(i32(7), Node(x : j, next : .None));
    j = (j + i32(1));
  });
  // Map holds exactly one entry (key 7); every replaced Node must have been
  // freed. Post-fix the live tracked count is a small constant; the pre-fix
  // leak made it grow with the loop count. Bound well under the loop count.
  assert(Gc.tracked_count() < u64(10), "hashmap same-key overwrite leaked the replaced value");
  assert(m.len() == usize(1), "map holds exactly one entry");
  println(`hashmap-overwrite ok`);
});
export(main);
